.TH MQ 1 "October 2026" "mu 1.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
mu \- a declarative tmux experience
.SH SYNOPSIS
mq <command> [<argument>]

.SH DESCRIPTION
mu is a simple tool to provide a more declarative tmux experience.

.SH COMMANDS

.TP
.B new, nw, n NAME
create a new layout with NAME or edit a already existed one.

.TP
.B edit, ed, e
open the layouts directory with $EDITOR.

.TP 
.B attach, at, a [NAME]
attach to last session opened if no NAME is provided, else attach to the provided session.

.TP 
.B start, st, s [NAME]
start a new session based on layout NAME, if it is already running, just attach.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mu/config.kdl
configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/mu/base.kdl
base layout file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/mu/layouts/*.kdl
each layout file.

